Most meeting assistants listen quietly and send a summary afterwards. Anthropic's new Claude Meetings beta works differently on paper: Claude joins the call as a visible participant, can be asked questions during the meeting, and can start building a document while people talk. This post sets out what Anthropic says the beta does, who can use it, what it saves and what admins can control. Everything here comes from two Anthropic pages, and we flag the points those pages leave open.

*Disclosure: this post was drafted by Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic, and checked by a separate AI reviewer against the cited pages for figures, dates and wording. This is not a full human review. Claude Meetings is an Anthropic product, so the drafting assistant and the product's vendor are the same company. Stackbrook did not test the product and has no affiliate relationship with Anthropic at the time of writing. The header image is AI-generated.*

## What Claude Meetings is

According to Anthropic's announcement, dated 12 November 2026, Claude Meetings lets Claude join a video call as a visible participant. It follows the conversation, writes notes and action items, and can start work while the meeting is still going. Teammates can ask it questions out loud or in the chat, and by default it answers in writing. The Help Center release notes of the same date describe it in similar terms, saying Claude can take notes, answer questions and build artifacts such as docs, whiteboards and slides during the call.

The announcement gives a simple example. Someone says "Claude, start a doc for this plan", and Claude writes up what has been said so far. In another example, Claude asks for approval before looking up information, then posts the result in the meeting chat. Before the call ends, anyone can ask Claude to share a recap with the team.

## Who can use it, and on what

The beta is not for everyone yet. Both pages say it is rolling out on Team and Enterprise plans, and the release notes add that it is in Claude and Claude Desktop. The announcement does not mention Free, Pro or Max plans, so we cannot say whether they will get it.

Only one video platform is supported today. Anthropic says support is currently available for Google Meet, with other platforms listed as coming soon. The announcement also says the beta is not available to some organisations, including those with zero data retention, a HIPAA-ready configuration or customer-managed encryption keys. If your company relies on one of those setups, the page suggests you will not see the feature for now.

Admins hold the switches. On Team plans, the ability to invite Claude is on by default and an admin can turn it off. On Enterprise plans, an admin turns it on for all or part of the organisation. Claude joins when someone adds it to a call, or when auto-join is switched on.

![Flow diagram of the checks that decide whether Claude can join a call in the Claude Meetings beta](/images/site1/claude-meetings-beta-explained-what-team-enterprise-get-chart.svg)
